From 707393bd95e1e1a4af3c36ff0a1adbf924eb92fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:40:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plans): a plan whose JSON text has a slip is mended, not
 lost (4522)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The daily check counted six propose_task_plan calls in four days refused
as „not valid JSON"; each run lost its plan. The tool log shows the parse
failing mid-text (position 148 of 270, 162 of 271, …), not at the end:
a slip in a whole plan, not a cut-off. The one fully visible case had a
lone quote before the routes' closing bracket (`}, "], "people_to_involve"`).

After a failed parse, four narrow repairs are tried in turn: drop U+FFFD,
close a Georgian „ that ended on an ASCII quote, drop a lone quote before
a bracket, drop a trailing comma. The result is used only if it parses,
and then passes every check a plan sent as an object passes. A plan that
really was cut off stays refused as before. No model-facing text changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
